{
  "name": "Enrich new leads in a Notion database with title, company and profile URL",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich new leads in a Notion database with title, company and profile URL\n\n### How it works\nTurn a bare email in Notion into a usable lead. The Notion Trigger checks your lead database every minute. New pages with an email, at most max_per_poll at a time, go to Argorant Enrich. When the person is found, the page gets their title, company and profile URL, and the Enriched checkbox is ticked, so you can filter the view. Pages without a match get the checkbox too, with an empty title, so they are not tried again.\n\nCosts: 1 credit per person found whose email passes the check. Misses and repeats are free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Add a Notion credential and share the lead database with that integration.\n4. Pick the database in **New page in the lead database** and check the property names in **Update the page** (Title, Company, Profile URL, Enriched).\n5. Set max_per_poll in **Settings** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a Seniority select property and map the seniority from the enrichment.",
